course: dictionary
lesson: 7729
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name more than one thing. The word puffin usually means a small black-and-white seabird with a big, bright orange and blue beak. Read the words around it to find out which puffin is meant.
explain: «Some breeds, like the Norwegian puffin dog, have six toes on each foot for climbing cliffs.» The clues are breeds, toes and climbing. A breed is a kind of dog, so here puffin is part of a dog's name, not a bird. Always ask: what does the sentence say this thing is?
explain: Some words are nicknames. A nickname is a friendly name that people use instead of the proper name. Puffins are called «sea parrot» and «clown of the sea» by some people, but these are nicknames, not the bird's real name.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the words around it.
fact: Puffin usually means a small seabird with an orange and blue beak and orange feet.
fact: The Norwegian puffin dog is a breed of dog, and its name contains the word puffin.
fact: Puffins nest in burrows on islands and cliffs in the North Atlantic, and they dive for fish such as sand eels.
fact: A nickname is a friendly name for someone or something, such as «sea parrot» for the puffin.
exercise: «Some breeds, like the Norwegian puffin dog, have six toes on each foot.» In this sentence, what kind of thing is the puffin dog? | A seabird | A cliff on an island | A kind of fish | *A breed of dog
exercise: What colour are a puffin's feet? | *Orange | Blue | White | Black
exercise: Where do puffins live? | Under the sea, on the seabed | In the middle of cities | In deserts | *On cliffs and islands
test: What is a nickname? | *A friendly name that is not the proper name | The colour of a bird's beak | A fish that a bird likes to eat | The home where a bird lays its eggs
test: «The puffin dived into the sea and came back with a fish in its beak.» What does dived mean? | Flew very high into the sky | Swam backwards to the shore | Slept on a rock | *Went head first under the water
exam: Ella reads «Some breeds, like the Norwegian puffin dog, have six toes on each foot.» What is a puffin in this sentence? | *Part of a dog's name | A bird with orange feet | A fish that dives for sand eels | A high cliff on an island
